# Google Colab environment, shared by every project in this repo.
# In Colab, copy this file to .env so main() picks it up automatically.
# From the repo root (%cd CodeCS4337Fall2026):
#   !cp .envcolab .env
# (starternotebook.ipynb does this for you.)
# Dataset lives on the fast local VM disk (re-downloaded each session).
# Outputs go to Google Drive so they survive runtime resets; requires
#   from google.colab import drive; drive.mount("/content/drive")
# Each project writes to <OUTPUT_DIR>/<ProjectName>/<config>/<timestamp>/.
DATA_DIR=/content/data
OUTPUT_DIR=/content/drive/MyDrive/CodeCS4337Fall2026/runs

# -----Lit Logger setup-----:
# LitLogger (optional, LitTrainingBasicConvnet with "litlogger": true):
# You get the key from your Lightning AI account in the browser.
# 1. Sign in at lightning.ai.
# 2. Click your profile picture in the top-right corner and open Global Settings.
# 3. Choose Keys in the left sidebar.
# 4. Under Programmatic access, the Login via CLI box shows both values.
# 5. Copy them into .env at the repo root:

# You need to setup following if you are using litlogger
# LIGHTNING_USER_ID=your-user-id
# LIGHTNING_API_KEY=your-api-key

# Do NOT put your Lightning AI keys in this file: it is tracked by git, so they
# would be pushed to GitHub. In Colab, store them as Secrets instead (key icon
# in the left sidebar), named LIGHTNING_USER_ID and LIGHTNING_API_KEY, with the
# values from lightning.ai -> profile picture -> Global Settings -> Keys ->
# "Login via CLI". Then run the "Load API keys" cell of starternotebook.ipynb
# (after the setup cells, before running a project): it copies them to .env.
# Locally, put the two lines in .env instead (not tracked by git).
# -----Lit Logger setup ends here-----:

# -----W&B setup-----:
# W&B (optional, LitWBTrainingBasicConvnet). Without a key, or if the login
# fails, runs are logged offline and print a `wandb sync ...` command to
# upload them later.
# You get the key from your W&B account in the browser:
# 1. Sign in (or sign up for free) at wandb.ai.
# 2. Open wandb.ai/authorize and copy the API key.
# 3. Locally, put it in .env at the repo root (not tracked by git):

# WANDB_API_KEY=your-api-key

# Do NOT put your W&B key in this file: it is tracked by git, so it would be
# pushed to GitHub. In Colab, store it as a Secret instead (key icon in the
# left sidebar) named WANDB_API_KEY. Then run the "Load API keys" cell of
# starternotebook.ipynb (after the setup cells, before running a project): it
# copies the key to .env, so notebook and terminal runs both find it.
# -----W&B setup ends here-----:
